<rml>
<head>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="theme.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="character_preview.rcss"/>
</head>
<body data-model="character_preview">
    <!-- P5: the new-character preview portrait frame (character_preview_window).
         The character is a GPU sprite drawn underneath; this doc only provides the
         curses-replacement chrome — a bordered box with a centred "CHARACTER
         PREVIEW" title strip. The box centre is TRANSPARENT so the sprite shows
         through; C++ sets #cp-box left/top/width/height each redraw to track the
         preview rect (and hides it when the terminal is too narrow). Passive
         (non-interactive) backdrop. -->
    <div id="cp-box" class="cp-box">
        <div class="cp-title" data-rml="title_rml"></div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
